A lens the author did not write, which would copy an optional field into a
required one and produces nothing for another required field. Both
diagnostics are about the block the author has to write, and each help
writes all of it.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	a:  string
	b?: int
}
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	a: string
	b: int
	c: bool
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	a: string
	b: int
	c: bool
}
-- out/error --
error[E0343]: b is optional in v0.0 and required in v1.0
 --> history/1.0.thema:5:1
  |
3 |     b: int
  |     - v1.0 requires b
...
5 | }
  | ^
  |
  = help: write ForwardLens: {v0_0: _, v1_0: {c: <mapping>, b: _coalesce(v0_0.b, <fallback>)}} in history/1.0.thema

error[E0346]: v1.0 has no ForwardLens, and v1.0 requires c
 --> history/1.0.thema:5:1
  |
5 | }
  | ^
  |
  = help: write ForwardLens: {v0_0: _, v1_0: {c: <mapping>, b: _coalesce(v0_0.b, <fallback>)}} in history/1.0.thema
